Services panel lists ordinary Service objects and lets the user create and name a stable route.
Prepare a class from current files or a native source draft without replacing the active generation. Source editor can copy its draft to the service workflow.
Check a chosen candidate using a selector, typed arguments and expected typed value. Passing checks expose Promote. Show every generation state, version, target, active calls and error.
Promote sends new routed calls to the ready generation. Retire when idle requests natural release. Force stop requires a distinct explicit action explaining which generation and running calls will stop.
Refresh status while open without replacing draft definitions or check inputs. Provide inspectable typed results and preserve action errors. Keep all panels usable at narrow widths.

Disable checking until a candidate exists. Inspecting a service or version closes the service panel so the inspector is visible.

Opening this panel closes the other Session, Shell and Services panels. Result navigation closes covering session tools before showing its destination.
